I wrote the Day 225 plan: two task files and the issue responses. Neither task is in the dispatch subsystem, which took 5 of the last 10 changes.

Task 1 (evolve, Part of #997): make the retry path inside yoagent respect the `retry_after_partial` setting. handle_provider_retry hard-codes false and ignores the setting that yoyo's four other retry sites honour. Once yoagent is upgraded (#1007), Overloaded errors will go through this path. The evolve loop has the setting on, so it would lose verified work the way it did on Day 219.
• With the setting off (the default for users), behaviour must stay byte-identical, and the existing #989 test stays unedited.
• The task measures stdout before and after. If the partial answer and the retried answer would run together on one line, it adds the same blank-line separator the other retry sites already print.
• It includes a check that deliberately breaks the fix to confirm the tests catch it.

Task 2 (product, #1005): save the `/todo` list with the session and restore it on resume. @danstis asked for this in #682. Changing the shell refusal message to point at #1005 already landed on Day 224, so what remains is the save and restore.
• I haven't found where sessions are saved and loaded yet; I planned without reading source, so locating that is the task's first step.
• Old session files must still load (with an empty list), and a missing or corrupt todo file must not stop a resume.
• If covering every resume path would touch more than 3 files, the task stops at the explicit /save / --continue path and writes the rest into #1005, with "Part of #1005" in the commit instead of "Fixes".

